drumee-roles (1.0.29-1~trixie1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Anchor the source version to the release train, and publish for the first time.
    .
    drumee-release existed at 1.0.0-1~trixie1 while its own payload recorded
    DRUMEE_RELEASE=1.0.29, which made the anchor inert: every role declares
    `Depends: drumee-release (= ${binary:Version})` precisely so two containers of
    one deployment cannot come from two rows of the manifest, and that constraint
    was the same string for every release train. Two trains would also have
    produced two different drumee-release 1.0.0-1~trixie1 artifacts — the same
    version, different bytes, which reprepro refuses (and which already bit
    drumee-static at 1.0.4).
    .
    components.roles now tracks `release`, so a train bump re-syncs and rebuilds
    this package and the anchor names the train it belongs to.

 -- Drumee Packaging <packaging@drumee.com>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 20:44:13 +0200

drumee-roles (1.0.0-1~trixie1) trixie; urgency=medium

